Maternity Ward after her labor pain started.
After the amniotomy, she is placed in the left
lateral position and on supplemental oxygen by
nasal cannula, and intravenous fluids and
Syntocinon® (oxytocin) infusion are started. A
while later and during fetal heart auscultation, a
fetal heart rate (FHR) of 70 bpm is noted. CTG
is applied, which reveals a baseline fetal heart
rate of 140 bpm, dropping to 70 bom
periodically with each episode of bradycardia
lasting approximately three minutes. Which one
of the following is the most appropriate next
step in management?','{"A":"Fetal scalp blood sampling.","B":"Stop Syntocinon.","C":"Immediate cesarean delivery.","D":"Continuous CTG monitoring.","E":"Reposition to supine."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-7c40e781902b","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"4ba80f8cbe4df48953f5","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","source_page":4,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"4ba80f8cbe4df48953f5","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":4,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Obstetrics","stem":"Mary, 27 years old, was admitted to the\nMaternity Ward after her labor pain started.\nAfter the amniotomy, she is placed in the left\nlateral position and on supplemental oxygen by\nnasal cannula, and intravenous fluids and\nSyntocinon® (oxytocin) infusion are started. A\nwhile later and during fetal heart auscultation, a\nfetal heart rate (FHR) of 70 bpm is noted. CTG\nis applied, which reveals a baseline fetal heart\nrate of 140 bpm, dropping to 70 bom\nperiodically with each episode of bradycardia\nlasting approximately three minutes. Which one\nof the following is the most appropriate next\nstep in management?","options":{"A":"Fetal scalp blood sampling.","B":"Stop Syntocinon.","C":"Immediate cesarean delivery.","D":"Continuous CTG monitoring.","E":"Reposition to supine."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","curr