Australian hospital with acute-onset
Shortness of breath, tachycardia, and
sweating after a long-distance flight from
California. She is 34 weeks pregnant. On
examination, she has a blood pressure of
110/87 mmHg, a pulse rate of 110 bpm, and a
respiratory rate of 26 breaths per minute.
Heart and lung auscultation is clear. There is
no leg swelling, warmth, or tenderness.
Which one of the following is the best
investigation in this situation?','{"A":"CT pulmonary angiogram (CTPA).\n9g B Electrocardiography.","B":"Bilateral lower extermity Doppler\nultrasound.","C":"D-dimer.","D":"Ventilation-perfusion scan.","E":"OC"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-71b4b12329ac","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"bc32b4cc4a0a8616b2cc","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","source_page":126,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"2711d5b9049c9e997426","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":253,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"bc32b4cc4a0a8616b2cc","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS  (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":126,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Obstetrics","stem":"A 32-year-old female presented in a regional\nAustralian hospital with acute-onset\nShortness of breath, tachycardia, and\nsweating after a long-distance flight from\nCalifornia. She is 34 weeks pregnant. On\nexamination, she has a blood pressure of\n110/87 mmHg, a pulse rate of 110 bpm, and a\nrespiratory rate of 26 breaths per minute.\nHeart and lung auscultation is clear. There is\nno leg swelling, warmth, or tenderness.\nWhich one of the following is the best\ninvestigation in this situation?","options":{"A":"CT pulmonary angiogram (CTPA).\n9g B Electrocardiography.","B":"Bilateral lower extermity Doppler\nultrasound.","C":"D-dimer.","D":"Ve