to the maternity unit at 38 weeks gestation
after a spontaneous rupture of the
membrane. On vaginal examination, the
cervix is 5 cm dilated and the membranes are
ruptured. Meconium-stained liquor is noted
in the vagina. A cardiotocography (CTG)
unveils a fetal heart rate of 130 bpm,
variability of 5 bpm, and variable
decelerations. Which one of the following
would be the most appropriate next step in
