become pregnant. She is extremely
concerned about rubella infection during
pregnancy and its impacts on her
baby because two years ago, her elder sister
had to undergo an abortion after she was
diagnosed with rubella infection. She
remembers that she was vaccinated for
measles, mumps, and rubella when she was a
child. Which one of the following statements
